From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Accept a NULL time format in the media source's
 Start.

IMFMediaSource::Start documents pguidTimeFormat as "Reserved; must be
NULL or GUID_NULL", but media_source_Start() dereferenced it: a caller
passing NULL crashed in IsEqualIID() (access violation reading 0x0).
A NULL time format is now the default one (GUID_NULL).

Game impacted: KanColle Arcade (Sega Nu): it starts its VC-1 WMV
attract movies through Media Foundation with a NULL time format, and
crashed when the first one played.
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -2020,14 +2020,14 @@
 
     if (source->state == SOURCE_SHUTDOWN)
         hr = MF_E_SHUTDOWN;
-    else if (!(IsEqualIID(time_format, &GUID_NULL)))
+    else if (time_format && !IsEqualIID(time_format, &GUID_NULL))
         hr = MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_TIME_FORMAT;
     else if (SUCCEEDED(hr = source_create_async_op(SOURCE_ASYNC_START, &op)))
     {
         struct source_async_command *command = impl_from_async_command_IUnknown(op);
         command->u.start.descriptor = descriptor;
         IMFPresentationDescriptor_AddRef(descriptor);
-        command->u.start.format = *time_format;
+        command->u.start.format = time_format ? *time_format : GUID_NULL;
         PropVariantCopy(&command->u.start.position, position);
 
         hr = MFPutWorkItem(source->async_commands_queue, &source->async_commands_callback, op);
